+  // fix is at the source, below.
+  //
+  // THE HSIO GUARD (the source). See the ge_hsio_guard cvar comment for the
+  // full anatomy. This is not a heuristic ledger writer (the M-077 class): the
+  // flag is a boot-time constant whose only legitimate writer runs once at
+  // device init and, under ReXGlue, always writes 0. A nonzero read is
+  // corruption, and restoring 0 is restoring truth. This hook runs on the
+  // guest thread that also runs the command-buffer kick, so there is no
